2.0 Purpose and Scope
2.1 Purpose  

Provide a standard operating procedure for creating an ad‑hoc ITSI Service, mapping KPIs, building correlation searches to generate Notables, and configuring alert actions (email, webhook, Slack, PagerDuty).
2.2 Scope and Applicability  

Applies to DHA ITSI administrators, SOC engineers, and service owners responsible for monitoring and incident generation.
2.3 Definitions and Acronyms  

KPI: Key Performance Indicator
Notable: ITSI notable event
SLA: Service Level Agreement
SPL: Search Processing Language
3.0 Roles and Responsibilities
3.1 Service Owner — defines runbook, acceptance criteria, and owner contact.
3.2 ITSI Administrator — creates services, KPIs, correlation searches, and configures alert actions.
3.3 SOC/On‑Call Team — responds to Notables, follows runbook and escalations.
3.4 Incident Manager — coordinates incident handling and RCA.
3.5 Stakeholders — business owners, application owners, and third-party contacts.

4.0 Prerequisites and Preconditions
4.1 Access & Permissions — ITSI admin role, access to Incident Review, Correlation Search creation rights.
4.2 Integrations — SMTP, Slack webhook, PagerDuty integration configured (placeholders used).
4.3 Naming Conventions — Service: Adhoc_Service_; KPI: Adhoc_KPI; Correlation: Adhoc_Corr_.
4.4 Security — do not include PII in email bodies; use secure webhooks.

5.0 Overview of Process
5.1 Workflow: Define goal → Create Service → Create KPI (or saved search) → Create Correlation Search → Configure Alert Actions → Test → Monitor → Promote/Cleanup.
5.2 Key metrics: count, recentTime, duration, status, kpi_value.

