7.0 Detailed SOP: Creating KPIs
7.1 Option A — From saved search (recommended)

Create saved search in Settings → Searches, Reports, Alerts → New
Saved search returns Entity, KPI value (0 OK, 1 problem), and relevant fields.
In Service → Add KPI → Create from Saved Search → map fields → set Calculation Window (e.g., 15m) and Cadence (e.g., 1m).
7.2 Option B — Create quick KPI saved search (SPL example)

Example KPI SPL (Missing source within 15m):
index=cloud-aws earliest=-15m host="splunk-httpinput.health.mil" (sourcetype="aws:elb:accesslogs" OR sourcetype="aws:audit:logs" OR sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" OR sourcetype="aws:route53")
| stats latest(_time) AS recentTime count BY source,sourcetype
| eval age = now() - recentTime
| eval kpi_value = if(isnull(recentTime) OR age>900, 1, 0)
| where kpi_value==1
| table source sourcetype kpi_value recentTime

Save as Adhoc_KPI__

7.3 KPI Configuration

Map Entity field: source (or transaction_name), KPI Value: kpi_value, Timestamp: recentTime.
Calculation window: 15 minutes; Cadence: 1 minute (adjust per SLA).
8.0 Detailed SOP: Creating Correlation Searches & Notables
8.1 Create Correlation Search

ITSI → Configure → Correlation Searches → Create New
Name: Adhoc_Corr__
App/Owner: ITSI / ops@example.mil
Description: Purpose, service mapping, runbook link
8.2 Define Search

Option 1: Reference saved KPI search (recommended)
Option 2: Paste SPL directly: use the KPI SPL or tstats-based SPL (fast) below.
8.3 Example tstats-based SPL (fast)
| tstats count latest(_time) AS recentTime WHERE index=cloud-aws AND host="splunk-httpinput.health.mil" AND (sourcetype="aws:elb:accesslogs" OR sourcetype="aws:audit:logs" OR sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" OR sourcetype="aws:route53") BY source,sourcetype
| eval age = now() - recentTime
| eval max_age = case(sourcetype=="aws:elb:accesslogs",900, sourcetype=="aws:audit:logs",900, sourcetype=="aws:cloudtrail",900, sourcetype=="aws:route53",900, true(),86400)
| eval status = case(isnull(recentTime),"Missing", age > max_age,"Missing", true(),"OK")
| eval duration = if(status=="Missing", tostring(age,"duration"), "0s")
| eval LatestEvent = if(isnull(recentTime),"Never",strftime(recentTime,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"))
| eval kpi_value = if(status=="OK",0,1)
| where kpi_value==1
| table source, sourcetype, status, duration, LatestEvent, recentTime, max_age, kpi_value

8.4 Notable Mapping & Threshold

Notable Condition: when kpi_value==1 OR status=="Missing"
Map fields: source → result.source, sourcetype → result.sourcetype, duration, LatestEvent, kpi_value, max_age.
8.5 Assign to Service and set Priority

Service: Adhoc_Service__
Severity: High (Missing), Medium (Warning), Low (OK)
Owner: SOC team / Owner contact
9.0 Alert Actions & Notification Configuration
9.1 Create Notable (default) — required.

9.2 Email Template (Replace placeholders)
To: derrick@example.mil
Subject: [ALERT] Adhoc_Service_ — Missing Data for $result.source$ / $result.sourcetype$
Body:
Alert: Adhoc_Service_ — Missing Data
Source: $result.source$
Sourcetype: $result.sourcetype$
Status: $result.status$
Duration: $result.duration$
LatestEvent: $result.LatestEvent$
Action: Follow runbook [runbook URL]. Escalate if unresolved after 30 minutes.

9.3 Slack Webhook (JSON payload example)
{
  "text": "[ALERT] Adhoc_Service_ — Missing Data",
  "attachments": [
    {
      "title": "$result.source$ / $result.sourcetype$",
