    }
  ]
}

9.4 PagerDuty (example)

Map notable severity to PagerDuty service key and urgency (high = P1). Use ITSI Alert Action integration.
9.5 Run Script / Automation

Optional: call remediation playbooks or ticket creation scripts. Provide path and parameters and test in staging.
9.6 Throttling, Aggregation & Suppression

Aggregate by: source + sourcetype
Suppression window: 30 minutes (configurable)
Escalation: if not acknowledged in 30 minutes → page on-call.
10.0 Testing & Validation
10.1 Test Plan

Test Case 1: Trigger missing condition (simulate missing events) → verify Notable creation, email, Slack, PagerDuty.
Test Case 2: Duplicate events within suppression window → verify no duplicate alerts.
Test Case 3: Recovery (events resume) → verify auto-resolve or close notable as configured.
10.2 Validation Checklist

 Notable appears in Incident Review
 Email delivered to derrick@example.mil
 Slack message posted to #team-alerts
 PagerDuty event created and routed
 Aggregation key functioning
 Throttle suppression working
10.3 Troubleshooting

No email: verify SMTP settings and mail server logs.
Missing fields: confirm SPL returns mapped fields and correlation search maps correctly.
No Slack: confirm webhook URL and connectivity.
11.0 Monitoring, Tuning, & Maintenance
11.1 Monitor for 24–72 hours, review false positives/negatives.
11.2 Tune max_age, cadence, and suppression windows.
11.3 If stable, promote to permanent service: rename, update runbook, and assign permanent owner.
11.4 If temporary, schedule cleanup and export config before deletion.

12.0 Incident Response & Escalation
12.1 Incident Review: owner triages Notable, follows runbook, and logs actions.
12.2 Escalation Matrix (example)

T0 (Immediate): SOC Analyst / on-call
T30 min: Incident Manager (pager)
T60 min: Service Owner / App Owner
T120 min: Major Incident Team / Leadership
12.3 Post Incident Actions

Create RCA, update runbook with lessons learned, and adjust thresholds.
13.0 Documentation, Archiving & Audit
13.1 Export correlation and KPI configs (UI → Export) and store in repo.
13.2 Archive test results, emails, and runbook revisions.
13.3 Keep audit logs for compliance (retention per DHA policy).

14.0 Security & Privacy Considerations
14.1 Do not include PII in alert content.
14.2 Use secure channels for webhooks (HTTPS).
14.3 Limit access to ITSI admin functions to required roles.

